id: E03
target: src/sello/ed25519.nim
desc: pointDecode: sign-bit reconciliation condition inverted, 'if sign: feNeg(x, x)' -> 'if not sign: feNeg(x, x)' -- negates x on the branch where the wire sign bit is CLEAR (root already matches, no negation needed) and leaves it un-negated when the sign bit is SET (a negation was needed), decoding every valid nonzero-x point to its negation. Re-cut (RFC-004 slice 1c: since feSqrtRatioM1's root is already guaranteed nonnegative, the old compare-then-maybe-negate 'feIsNegative(x) != sign' collapsed to a plain 'if sign' conditional negate -- the compare this mutant used to flip no longer exists to flip, so the same defect class (wrong-branch negation) is re-cut onto the new condition instead.
====OLD====
  if sign:
    feNeg(x, x)
====NEW====
  if not sign:
    feNeg(x, x)
====END====
